From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Aug 30 05:55:28 2000
From: Nikola Milutinovic <Nikola.Milutinovic () ev ! co ! yu>
Date: Wed, 30 Aug 2000 05:55:28 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Linking problems on T64 UNIX 4.0F
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96761483131727

Hi all.

Andrew Hobson <ahobson@eng.mindspring.net> hit the nail on the head.

|> # cc -c -shared test.c 
|
|> # ld -oldstyle_liblookup -L/usr/local/lib -ldb -o test.exe test.o
|> ld:
|> Error: Undefined:
|> db_create
|
|You didn't tell the linker that you wanted to use a shared library.
|Try the -call_shared option.
|
|$ ld -call_shared -L/usr/local/lib  -o test test.o -ldb -lc
|
|The -v option to cc and ld can shed some light.  Try this:
|
|$ cc -v -L/usr/local/lib -ldb test.c -o proba.exe

This worked. Thanks to all others who responded.

