Subject: SUMMARY : Compaq 35/70 GB DLT tape +  Tru64 5.0A = unable to writ	e to
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96758461026093

Thanks to everybody who helped me with the above

briefly
-------
the problem turned out to be an incorrect cable - a differential 
SCSI cable had been used instead of a non-differential cable

details
-------

After I posted, further inspection revealed lines like

Aug 24 11:32:15 vmunix: scsi0: SCSI Error for target 10 sist0 = 0x4
Aug 24 11:32:33 vmunix: scsi0: SCSI Error for target 10 sist0 = 0x4

in /var/adm/messages

(target 10 = the tape device) , and using the scu utility : 

scu> verify media starting 100 records 100
Verifying 51200 bytes on /dev/ntape/tape2 (DLT7000), please be patient...
scu: 'verify tape' failed on device 'DLT7000' at nexus [0/10/0]
scu: Sense Key = 0x8 = BLANK CHECK - No-data condition occured,
     Sense Code/Qualifier = (0, 0x5) = End-of-data detected
scu: Error number 1 occurred on Mon Aug 28 12:26:58 2000

and finally somebody realised the cable could be incorrect. 

(Didn't think of cable initially as communication with device
did work up to a point)

Several people suggested using DLTTape IV rather than IIIXT with this
drive and I have followed up on this, it seems to work well now that the 
correct cable is installed.

Thanks again to all those who helped out.

Cheers

Alan McCulloch

