To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Libcurses question
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96752479701600


	My thanks to Paul Roetman, Chewy and Hoai Tran for replying so quickly.
The basic gist was no, the libcurses libraries between version 4 and 5 are
not compatiable.  I was in the process of hunting around for some I could
install when I bumped into an sys admin for another department who put me
on another trail.

	The version 5 libcurses were already installed under
/usr/shlib/libcurses.so, but programs were asking for it in
/usr/shlib/osf.1/libcurses.so  It turned out to be because the program were
"standard" installs that had been compilied under version 4.0  Rather than
face the hassle of having to recompile and install the programs for our
version 5 machines and then run seperate mounts for v4 and v5 (Probably the
preferred option).  I just left the version 4 libcurses.so in
/usr/shlib/osf.1  He thinks that version 4 apps will look for it there and
version 5 apps will look for it un /usr/shlib.

	How good a solution this is, I have not idea, but I'm just happy it all
seems to work...

	Cheers, 
		Ryan.

