I could download the latest version (5.8) from:
ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Alpha/firmware/v5.8/

Also, Bryan Lavelle from Compaq stated that I did need to run the
ECO (EISA Configuration Utility) and that it was proprietary software
that I needed to purchase.  If I need it, shouldn't it be supplied with
the hardware/OS?  I found a copy in our software library and ran it.

Well, that solved the problem with the messages at during initialization
but now I no longer have a valid bootable disk.  I tried booting from
the CD and relabeling but then a fsck trashed the filesystem throwing
everything into 'lost+found'.  I intend to just restore are rerun the
