Hello again,

thanks to Larry Clegg, Bob Klenotiz and Matthias Dolder who
responded. Not to forget Alan Hinden from Compaq. 

Bob said that all KGPSA's had to be placed onto the same 
PCI bus. Matthias also said that the ES40 seems to be very picky 
about PCI bus placement of the KGPSA's and suggested to 
unplug ONE of them. I removed the Fibre on pgb and yes, 
the installation CD booted through! I could finish installing
V5.0A and the TCS SW. I then installed PK1 of V5.0A. This
brought the EMX FW to V1.22 and from then on I could boot
my systems with all KGPSA's connected. 

So thanks to all of you (especially -mad) who led me to the
right direction here. 

Regards, 

Arnold Sutter, UDT

>>>>>>>>>>>>> original message >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
Hello Managers, 

we tried all afternoon to boot with the V5.0A installation
CD an ES40 (V5.7-8x FW) with dual KGPSA-CA on a Multibus 
HSG80 (NSPOF config) on ACS 8.5F. 

The boot process did hang after displaying the third
IntraServer combo card entry on the console. 

Removing the KGPSA's from the FC fabric did not hang 
the system, but this left me with no disks to install 
