Subject: Summary: vdump error [13] on AdvFS volumes in single-user
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96580240118118

My problem was:
> I am trying to get a single-user backup of our system prior to
> installing the V5.0A patch 1 kit and I am getting the following
> errors:
>
> vdump: error [13] posting event: sys.unix.fs.advfs.fset.backup.lock
> rmfset: error [13] posting event: sys.unix.fs.advfs.fset.rm.lock
...
> Environment is Tru64 V5.0A, LSM and AdvFS 
> on a 500MHz DS20E with 4 x 9.1GB disk and a TZ877 tape drive.

The only response I got was from Dr Tom Blinn, who said:

> Looks like it's trying to use file locking that just hasn't been 
> turned on.  I have no idea whether the errors are serious or whether
> the utilities that are complaining went ahead and did what they were
> supposed to do.  You may get better results if you boot up to 
> multi-user, then shut down to single.
> Or boot to run level 2 but disable logins.

Doing the backup at run level 2 removed the error messages.

I suspect that the critical factor is that evmd is running at level 2.
The error message says "error [13] posting event", so it is reasonable
that this is caused by not having the event manager running.

The fact that both vdump and rmfset produced similar errors suggests
that the error was in event handling rather than core functions.

I checked the dumps on the tape, and they seem to be fine.

Blair Phillips
AirServices Australia
blair.phillips@airservices.gov.au

