From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Aug 17 22:24:27 2000
From: J S <act3000 () hotmail ! com>
Date: Thu, 17 Aug 2000 22:24:27 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Apache and KeepAlive
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96655102915015


>>Question
>>We are using an Apache Web Server for performance
>>testing.  During testing some clients seem to hang.

>>Reply

I have no idea if this is related, ... but.

When we first upgraded to Stronghold 2.3, based upon Apache, the server
hung, although it also hung up the clients.

For us, the solution was to set:

	MaxRequestsPerChild 300

We played with "KeepALive off", but found that once we made the above
change, we could turn KeepALive on and it solved the problem.

Regards, M. Tomkin

